\ Helper module for lexical_closure_capture.1z.
\
\ `val` deliberately collides with a local binding the main test defines, so a
\ closure that closes over the local must not resolve to this module word.
\ `apply` runs a passed quotation inside this module's body, which is what makes
\ this module's own `val` / `module-only` live on the frame stack while the
\ quotation executes.

val: ( -- s ) [ "MODULE-VAL" ] ;

module-only: ( -- s ) [ "MODULE-ONLY" ] ;

apply: ( q -- x ) [ call ] ;

\ Spawn a passed quotation from inside this module's body. This module's `val`
\ is live on the frame stack at the spawn, so the spawn-time frame clone carries
\ that module word into the child task above the caller's local frame.
apply-spawn: ( q -- ) [ spawn drop ] ;
